  m_text: In 1498 the Portuguese navigator Vasco da Gama reached Calicut. Within two centuries Portuguese, Dutch, French and British trading companies had set up posts along India's coasts. The British East India Company turned trade into conquest after the Battle of Plassey in 1757, and after the great uprising of 1857 the British Crown took direct control.
